@page "/about"

<PageTitle>How it's built | NATS Shop</PageTitle>

<div class="page-head">
    <div>
        <h1 class="title">How it's built</h1>
        <p class="lede">
            NATS Shop is a working storefront split into small .NET services. They never call each other over
            HTTP; every request becomes a NATS message, and the answer comes back the same way.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="about">
    <div class="prose">
        <h2>The path of one request</h2>
        <p>Here's what happens when you add a keyboard to your cart:</p>
        <ol class="path">
            <li><strong>Your browser</strong><span>This Blazor WebAssembly app sends an HTTP request with your session ID.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Gateway</strong><span>An ASP.NET Core API asks the products service for the item over NATS, then sends the cart update as a second NATS request.</span></li>
            <li><strong>NATS</strong><span>The broker hands each message to one free instance of the right service (queue groups).</span></li>
            <li><strong>Cart service</strong><span>Writes the updated cart to Valkey.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Reply</strong><span>The answer travels back over NATS to the gateway and then to the browser.</span></li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Why it's fast</h2>
        <p>
            NATS keeps a connection open between services, so there's no per-call HTTP setup between them.
            Each service does one job and holds its data close: products in PostgreSQL, carts in Valkey.
        </p>
        <p>
            The readout in the header measures the full round trip from this browser, so you can see the speed for
            yourself. Select it to see the most recent requests.
        </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="stack" aria-labelledby="stack-heading">
        <h2 id="stack-heading">Stack</h2>
        <dl class="specs">
            <dt>Runtime</dt>
            <dd>.NET 10</dd>
            <dt>Frontend</dt>
            <dd>Blazor WebAssembly</dd>
            <dt>Messaging</dt>
            <dd>NATS 2.15</dd>
            <dt>Products</dt>
            <dd>PostgreSQL 18, EF Core</dd>
            <dt>Carts</dt>
            <dd>Valkey 9.1</dd>
            <dt>Services</dt>
            <dd>Gateway, Products, Cart, Recommendations</dd>
            <dt>Deploys to</dt>
            <dd>Docker Compose, Kubernetes</dd>
        </dl>
    </aside>
</div>
